//ENVIRONMENT
title: Light_Check
---
<<declare $light_on = true>>
<<if $light_on>>
    Turn off the light?

    -> Yes
        <<light_off DialogueManager>>
        <<set $light_on = false>>
        You flicked the switch off.
    -> No
        You decided to leave it on.

<<else>>
    Turn on the light?

    -> Yes
        <<light_on DialogueManager>>
        <<set $light_on = true>>
        You flicked the switch on.
    -> No
        You decided to leave it alone.
<<endif>>
===

title: PC
---
The computer won't turn on
Punch it?
-> Yes
    //Do whatever
    You punched the computer. It didn't respond. 
-> No
    You save your fist for another day
===

title: Bed
---
<<declare $has_key = false>>
There seem to be faint bloodstains on the bed ...
<<if $has_key == false>>
    You feel a strange hard object beneath the blankets
    Pull it out?
    -> Yes
        You pull out a small rusty key
        <<set $has_key = true>>
    -> No
        You decide against it
<<endif>>
===

title: Table
---
<<declare $has_documents = false>>
<<if $has_key>>
    <<if $has_documents == false>>
        You open the drawers with the rusty key. Inside are a set of documents.
        Take the documents? 

        -> Yes
            <<obtain_evidence GameManager "Documents">>
            <<set $has_documents = true>>
            Obtained Sealed Documents
        -> Leave them be
            You decided to leave the documents. Taking them could cause suspicion after all
    <<else>>
        The drawer is empty
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    You try to open the drawers, but they're locked
<<endif>>
===

title: Bottle
---
The bottle is filled with a dark, viscous liquid
===

//CHARACTER DIALOGUE
title: TestCharacter
---
<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Miku" "Miku2">>
Miku: Find anything yet?
Miku2: Nope. Haven't really looked, though.
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku" "angry">>
Miku: What?! I've been searching this whole time while you've just been standing there?!
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku2" "angry">>
Miku2: Well, nobody told you to do all the work.
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku" "sad">>
Miku: ...
Miku: Ugh. At this rate, we're never going to find it.
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku2" "sad">>
Miku2: Aw, don't be like that. Now that I'm helping, we'll find it in no time!
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku" "angry">>
Miku: Why you...
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku" "happy">>
<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Miku2" "angry">>
Miku: You're impossible, you know that?
<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
===

//Cutscene Testing
title: Cutscene
---
<<show_cutscene DialogueManager 0>>
I looked all over for her.
<<next_cutscene_image DialogueManager>>
All the places we used to go.
<<next_cutscene_image DialogueManager>>
But I just couldn't find her.
<<next_cutscene_image DialogueManager>>
Write something random.
<<next_cutscene_image DialogueManager>>
Next thing I knew...
<<next_cutscene_image DialogueManager>>
The day had come to an end
===


title: Sound
---
I am going to play a song.
<<play_music SoundManager act_1>> 
See?
Now I am going to change the song.
<<play_music SoundManager sneak>> 
The song has now changed
I'll now stop the song
<<stop_music SoundManager>>
Let's play a song and add some sfx
<<play_music SoundManager act_1>> 
<<play_sfx SoundManager tap>> 
Now that it's playing, let's play a one shot
<<play_sfx_one_shot SoundManager wash_face>>
Ok, let's stop the sfx
<<stop_sfx SoundManager>>
And stop the music
<<stop_music SoundManager>>


===

